WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:04.250
Rhiannon: Each time a new medication
is prescribed, a doctor or other

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:08.410
professional will not know how well it
is going to work until the individual

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:10.010
has been taking it for a while.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.960
It will also be difficult
to predict whether they will

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.809
suffer from any side effects.

00:00:15.639 --> 00:00:18.909
Not all medication works for every
person and many medications take

00:00:18.909 --> 00:00:23.970
time to start working and longer
to reach their full potential.

00:00:24.759 --> 00:00:28.669
Leah: All medications have side
effects, but not everyone gets them,

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:30.980
and each person is affected differently.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:35.830
Some side effects improve or go
away over time, some don’t happen

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:39.540
straight away, and some may seem as
bad as the illness being treated.

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:47.889
Rhiannon: An individual may need to try
a few different medications and different

00:00:47.889 --> 00:00:50.059
dosages before they find the right one.

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:54.959
Medication used to treat depression
for example, normally takes a few weeks

00:00:54.969 --> 00:00:57.300
to start having a beneficial effect.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:01.950
Leah: In most cases an individual has a
choice not to take a medication if they

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:06.910
don’t want to, but it can be worth a
try, to see if it can help and getting

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:10.310
a parent or carer to give support
and understand the treatment plan,

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:12.370
gives it the best chance of success.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.910
Rhiannon: If an individual’s mental
health problem is severe, it may be

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:20.700
that they ‘have to’ take the medication
to maintain good mental health.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:28.820
If medication works and makes improvements
to mental health, repeat prescriptions

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:32.980
will be issued, but regular monitoring
and occasional checkups will follow.

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:37.150
Leah: To find out more about different
medications available, and what they

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:40.789
are prescribed for, you can go to the
following link for further information.

00:01:40.789 --> 00:01:48.330
http://youngminds.org.uk/youngminds-professionals/our-projects/headmeds/

